    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "HVAC demand jumped this week. The team completed 57 jobs, 10 more than the 4-week average of 47.00, and revenue rose to $28,475.00, 22.7% above the average of $23,210.00. Almost all of the extra work was HVAC: 28 jobs against an average of 15.50 (23 of them repairs) and $16,880.00 in revenue against $8,120.00. Plumbing (17 jobs) and Electrical (12 jobs) were close to normal. Thursday was the busiest day with 12 jobs, and Saturday still had 7.\n\nQuality slipped as volume rose. Callbacks went from a 4-week average of 3.00 to 7, and 6 of them were HVAC, which is 21.4% of HVAC jobs. The first-time fix rate fell to 78.9% from an average of 87.8%. HVAC fixed 19 of 28 jobs first time (67.9%), while Plumbing and Electrical together fixed 26 of 29 (89.7%). The average rating dropped to 4.3 from 4.5.\n\nWhat to look at: the HVAC callbacks, starting with Owen B. (3 callbacks on 11 jobs) and Dana R. (2 callbacks on 10 jobs). Check whether repeat visits came from parts not on the van or from rushed first visits, and whether HVAC needs extra cover next week if demand stays high. Also fix the export: one job appears twice and 11 jobs have no rating, including 6 of 12 Electrical jobs."
    },
